# Repository instructions for coding agents

Keep this file short. It is always-on context.

## Mandatory boundaries
- Respect service/module ownership and existing architecture boundaries.
- Inspect actual code before changing behavior.
- Prefer the smallest coherent change.
- Do not introduce complex workarounds to bypass a broken requirement or contradictory contract.
- If a task requires materially broader architecture changes than requested, report the conflict before implementing.
- Do not perform unrelated refactors.
- Add or update tests for changed behavior when practical.

## Context discipline
- Search before broad reading.
- Read only files relevant to the current task.
- Do not load large generated files or historical documentation unless required.
- Summaries passed between agents must contain conclusions and exact file/symbol references, not source dumps.

## Project-specific rules
Add only stable, high-value architecture rules here. Put detailed service-specific rules in scoped instruction files rather than growing this file.
